(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/doc_type "adr")
  (:adr/id "adr-2609112107-reservation-cljk-host-loader-contract")
  (:adr/topic "cljk-host-loader")
  (:adr/title "Proposed managed Node loader contract for canonical .cljk reservation sources")
  (:adr/status "proposed")
  (:adr/date "2026-09-11")
  (:adr/body "Scope: a reviewable loader extension contract, not an implemented loader or authorization to deploy. Global nbb and the shared checkout are unchanged. No diagnostic mirror is an execution or release artifact.\n\nObserved managed entrypoint: root package.json pins nbb 1.4.208; scripts/nbb-run-tests.cljs ultimately invokes require and scripts/nbb_compat.cljs is a maintenance bridge. No managed nbb fork or installed kbb executable was found in this investigation. amu's project_files compiler resolver accepts .cljk, but that does not establish an arbitrary Node host replacement.\n\nOfficial nbb v1.4.208 source: https://github.com/babashka/nbb/blob/v1.4.208/src/nbb/core.cljs find-file-on-classpath searches .cljs/.cljc/.clj within each classpath directory; handle-libspecs calls it for unresolved names and reload. https://github.com/babashka/nbb/blob/v1.4.208/src/nbb/api.cljs initialize/loadFile/loadString expose no source resolver option. registerModule registers JavaScript modules. Internal register-plugin! merges SCI context options, but handle-libspecs performs its own source search. No supported public hook that replaces this path was established. Preloading a namespace, monkey-patching minified private names, or copying renamed sources would not satisfy this contract.\n\nPreferred candidate: propose a supported source-resolver option at nbb.core/find-file-on-classpath, passed through nbb.api/initialize, and publish a reviewed version through the existing managed package pin. A supported host exposing equivalent transitive source resolution is an alternative only after the same acceptance suite passes. A maintained fork would require an explicit ownership/release decision; this draft creates no fork and advances no pin. Changing only scripts/nbb-run-tests.cljs is insufficient because run.cljk and ref_race.cljk bypass that runner.\n\nResolution contract: input includes absolute ordered classpath roots, explicit repository ownership boundaries and cljk-origin.edn files, target :cljs, namespace, reload flag. Return a canonical absolute existing source path, its declared origin and repository identity, or a typed resolution error. Preserve classpath-root precedence. Within the first root with namespace candidates, use the manifest to map .cljk paths back to their pre-rename relative namespace paths; do not guess platform from collision suffix names. Node preference is declared .cljs then .cljc; declared .clj alone is target-incompatible. Reader features remain :org.babashka/nbb and :cljs. A .cljs.cljk or .clj.cljk collision path is selected by its manifest origin, not by lexical order. Two candidates at the same platform rank reject as ambiguous. Existing legacy source and renamed source at the same rank also reject. Do not skip an invalid first-root candidate to silently load a later root.\n\nFail closed: reject absent/unknown origin for a .cljk candidate, unsupported manifest format, duplicate keys, duplicate namespace/rank, stale missing file, escaping/absolute manifest path, mismatched collision suffix and origin, or symlink escaping its declared repository. Discover ownership via explicitly registered source repositories; do not inherit an unrelated ancestor manifest. Cache only against repository and manifest identity plus source metadata; reload must observe changed manifests. Legacy-only roots retain existing nbb ordering; strict behavior applies when renamed candidates participate. Errors distinguish not-found, invalid-origin, ambiguous-source, target-incompatible and invalid-manifest and report candidate paths without reading secrets.\n\nTransitive behavior: the same resolver handles entrypoint policy validation, ns :require, require, use where supported, nested requires, macro requires under existing nbb semantics, and :reload. No regex dependency pre-scan or topological preload. Resolution must preserve source bytes, source path diagnostics, aliases/refers, asynchronous require completion, and existing cycle/error behavior.\n\nRequired conformance cases (not yet executed on an implemented loader): A.cljk requires B.cljk requires C.cljk; cljs/cljc/clj collisions select cljs on Node and cljc when cljs absent; clj-only rejects; absent/unknown/duplicate origin and same-rank candidate reject; manifest traversal and escaping symlink reject; first-root precedence and no invalid-root fallback; .reload rereads canonical changed source; legacy-only ns retains behavior; source exception path identifies original .cljk. Each case must exercise the real host, not just a resolver helper.\n\nCanonical acceptance: use only source-repository paths to execute inga-node script/run.cljk, script/test.cljk, script/ref_race.cljk, script/test-archive.cljk and inga script/test-reservation.cljk. run must use disposable test identity/data and local test endpoints only; assert start/stop rather than timeout success. Tests must await completion. Include archive process restart and quorum-race loser assertions. Current nbb 1.4.208 attempts exit 1: test and test-archive cannot find their existing .cljk test namespaces; run and ref_race first fail at kotoba.lang.text, so those two also have an unresolved dependency-path condition. These failures are not passing qualification.\n\nDependencies: review loader proposal and establish supported host first; merge inga shared prefix/reservation next; integrate archive against a merged inga revision via the existing dependency mechanism; then rerun canonical acceptance before considering readiness. The diagnostic mirror passed archive 7 tests/39 assertions, foundation 80/858 and node 33/106, but is logic evidence only. No unmerged dependency pins, deployment, credentials, live Kotobase writes or money movement are part of this draft.")
))
